> admissible point. The estimates below come from per-call costs only.{{endif}}

**Per-call costs under the other instruments.** For comparison, the request rate at
which one core would be fully busy with registrar-core work alone, at the same request
mix, from the simulated runs and the pacing check:

{{table:capacity_provisional}}

From the microbenchmarks alone (§6.1), one core executes about
{{cap.micro.RegisterFresh/N=1000/T=16.ops_per_s|sig:2}} fresh registrations/s (N = 1000, T = 16),
{{cap.micro.RandomNodes/N=1000/T=16.ops_per_s|sig:2}} lookups/s at T = 16 and
{{cap.micro.RandomNodes/N=5000/T=64.ops_per_s|sig:2}} lookups/s at T = 64.
{{if:share.cgo.total_ns}}A full `REGTOPIC` costs about {{share.cgo.total_ns|sig:2}} ns once validation is included (§6.1),
so a core spent only on `REGTOPIC` handling would serve about
{{share.cgo.regtopic_per_core|sig:2}} requests/s; validation, not the registrar core, sets that
limit.{{endif}}
